pedia/thumbs/philippe-bunau-varilla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Philippe Bunau-Varilla</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Philippe Bunau-Varilla was a French engineer who worked on Ferdinand de Lesseps's failed Panama canal and later lobbied the United States to buy the French company's…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/philippe-de-rullecourt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippe-de-rullecourt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Philippe de Rullecourt</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Philippe de Rullecourt was a French adventurer and soldier who styled himself baron.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/philippe-guerrier"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippe-guerrier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Philippe Guerrier</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Philippe Guerrier (1757–1845) was a Haitian general who served as president from May 1844 until his death in April 1845.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/philippe-leclerc-de-hauteclocque"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippe-leclerc-de-hauteclocque.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Philippe Leclerc de Hauteclocque</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Philippe Leclerc de Hauteclocque was a French general who joined the Free French in 1940.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/philippe-pastour-de-costebelle"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/philippe-pastour-de-costebelle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Philippe Pastour de Costebelle</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span>